# NO LINE-ENDING TRANSLATION, ANYWHERE IN THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# Several things here are identified by the SHA-256 of their exact bytes:
#
#   * the vendored RBA inputs under data/raw/, checked by
#     tests/test_submission.py::test_the_frozen_structured_inputs_match_their_pinned_hashes
#     against data/raw/checksums.json;
#   * the minutes corpus, whose fingerprint is part of `call_config_hash()` - so a
#     changed byte moves the Words cache directory and discards every committed envelope;
#   * the frozen panel and tier files, fingerprinted into the Shock stage hash.
#
# Git's default on Windows (`core.autocrlf=true`) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. The
# blob is unchanged, so the repository looks fine, but the file on disk is not the file
# that was hashed: a student cloning on Windows failed the frozen-input check on a clean
# clone, having done nothing wrong. `-text` tells Git to hand over the bytes it stored.
#
# This applies to EVERY file rather than only the hashed ones, because the set of hashed
# files has grown twice and a list is one more thing to forget to update.
* -text

# And the genuinely binary formats, stated explicitly so no future setting re-enables
# translation or attempts a textual diff on them.
*.parquet binary
*.joblib binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.m4a binary
